{title: Everything That Breathes}
{subtitle: Psalm 150}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 125}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Praise the Lord in his sanctuary
Praise him in the mighty heavens
Praise him for his powerful deeds
Praise him for his surpassing greatness
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let [Abmaj7]every[Eb/G]thing [Abmaj7]that [Eb/G]has [Eb]breath
Praise the Lord, praise the Lord
Let [Abmaj7]every[Eb/G]thing [Abmaj7]that [Eb/G]has [Eb]breath
Praise the Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Praise him with the trumpet blast
Praise him with the harp and lyre
Praise him with the tambourine and dancing
Praise him with the strings and pipe
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let [Abmaj7]every[Eb/G]thing that [Abmaj7]has breath
[Eb/G]Praise [Eb]the Lord, praise the Lord
Let everything that [Abmaj7]has breath
[Eb/G]Praise the [Abmaj7]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Clap [Eb/G]your [Eb]hands, crash the cymbals
Ring them loud, praise him [Abmaj7]louder
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb/G]Let ev[Abmaj7]erything [Eb/G]that [Eb]has breath
Praise the Lord, praise [Abmaj7]the Lord
[Eb/G]Let ev[Abmaj7]erything [Eb/G]that [Eb]has breath
Praise the Lord
{end_of_chorus}
